---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="Understand what GuideHollow stores locally, how browser tools and search work, and what GitHub Pages and external links may collect." breadcrumbs={[{name:'Privacy Policy',url:'/privacy-policy/'}]}>
<header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow mint">/ privacy_policy</p><h1>Your inputs<br />stay with you.</h1><p>Effective October 23, 2026. Updated November 4, 2026 to describe the four browser-only tools, static source notes, optional local claim-ledger TSV import/export, local scoring, saved-only exports, and best-effort leave warnings. This notice describes the site's current configuration.</p></header><article class="prose info-content"><h2>Who operates this site</h2><p>GuideHollow is maintained by emfls through the <a href="https://github.com/emfls/guidehollow">GuideHollow GitHub project</a>. Our available contact channel is described on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. The issue tracker is public; do not post sensitive details.</p><h2>Browser tools</h2><p>The AI Prompt Builder combines text locally in your browser. The response checklist tracks checkmarks locally in the open page. The Weighted Average Audit Workbench parses CSV text and calculates summaries locally inside your browser; it does not upload the CSV. The Source Claim Verifier includes the original fictional teaching notes directly in its static page, downloads a public fictional answer-key CSV from this website for interactive questions, and scores your selections locally without uploading the answers. Its separate manual claim ledger holds user-entered sources, claims, passages, verdicts and review reasons only in the page's memory; requesting a TSV download creates a temporary browser file link (the browser controls whether it is saved). If you choose to import a previously downloaded TSV, your browser reads that local file only in the current page and validates it before replacing existing review rows with your confirmation; no upload or server copy occurs. Leaving or reloading the page clears the entries. If there are saved rows or unfinished form fields, the browser may show a native leave warning, but some browsers do not show it. This does not save or transmit the entries. A TSV download includes saved rows only, not unfinished Add/Edit fields; the tool warns before exporting while a draft is present. Clear all reviews also removes any unfinished input text. We do not send these inputs to an AI service, backend, database, or analytics endpoint. Inputs and checkmarks are not intentionally saved between page loads. Your browser or extensions may independently provide form restoration.</p><p>Copying writes the selected output to your device clipboard when permitted. Downloading creates a text file on your device. Other apps or users of the device may be able to access these items.</p><h2>Search</h2><p>Search downloads a static index from this website and filters it in your browser. Search terms appear in the page URL. A search URL you open or share may be visible in browser history, hosting logs, and to someone who receives that link. Avoid entering confidential information in search.</p><h2>Local storage and cookies</h2><p>The site uses one localStorage entry, <code>gh-theme</code>, to remember an explicitly selected light or dark theme. Without that preference, it follows your system appearance. You can remove this setting through your browser's site storage controls. The site works if storage is unavailable.</p><p>GuideHollow does not currently set advertising or analytics cookies, load third-party fonts, run analytics, or display ads. We do not run user accounts, a mailing list, comments, or a contact form on this site.</p><h2>Hosting and external services</h2><p>GitHub Pages serves the website and may process technical information such as IP addresses and request details for security and operation. GitHub controls its own handling and retention of that data; see the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.</p><p>Links to GitHub and other external sites take you to services with their own policies. Submitting a public issue to GitHub sends the content and associated account information to GitHub. We do not control those services.</p>{site.contactEmail && <section><h2>Email correspondence</h2><p>If you contact us by email, your chosen email provider and the receiving provider process your address, message, and any attachments. Messages may contain personal information you choose to share. Send only what is needed to answer your request; do not send secrets or sensitive documents. Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> to ask about handling or removal of correspondence.</p></section>}<h2>Advertising, Google AdSense &amp; cookie disclosures</h2><p>An AdSense ownership-verification meta tag (on indexable content pages only) and <code>ads.txt</code> file are active on this site to verify publisher ownership. Ad requests remain gated off until approval and consent configuration are complete; an AdSense Publisher ID alone does not enable ad serving in this site.</p><p>Once Google AdSense display advertising is enabled on GuideHollow, third-party vendors, including Google, will use cookies (such as Google and DoubleClick advertising cookies), web beacons, or similar identifiers to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites on the internet, measure ad performance, and protect against invalid traffic. Learn more about <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses data from sites and apps that use its services</a>.</p><ul><li>Manage or opt out of Google personalized advertising at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google Ad Settings</a>.</li><li>Opt out of personalized advertising cookies from participating third-party vendors at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">YourAdChoices (aboutads.info)</a>.</li></ul><p>Before enabling live ad requests, we will ensure applicable regional consent choices are active alongside this notice.</p><h2>Your choices and questions</h2><p>You can browse without submitting information, disable JavaScript, remove local storage, and avoid external links. JavaScript is needed for interactive search, theme switching, copy buttons, and automatic tool behavior.</p><p>Use the public contact route for a general privacy question without including personal details. {site.contactEmail ? 'For a request that should not be public, use the email link on the contact page and provide only the information needed.' : 'A private contact channel and fuller operator information are still required before accepting confidential requests.'} We will revise this notice when site features or data practices change.</p></article>
</Base>
